{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2980","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2980","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2980\",\"parent_revision\":\"efac5275f77b6c0931a3535957ce1c1dfd40a791\",\"root_revision\":\"147eab68c4fc28898a9249d194ce4801adff2c9ba9fd29e25883dfebed15eba3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/groom-drift.md` (Mode B, ~line 81-83) and `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feasibility-gate.md` (~line 23) instruct a haiku agent to extract data from a `backlog view --selector \\\"{title}\\\"` response via `sections[\\\"Impact Radius\\\"]`, `sections[\\\"Files\\\"]`, and `sections['Priority']` \u2014 Title-Case string keys.\\n\\nObserved: for a title-based selector (not `#N`/issue URL/GitHub URL), `operations.view_item`'s `parse_issue_selector` returns `None`, so GitHub-body enrichment never runs, and the response's `sections` dict is built by `operations._build_sections_from_yaml_item`, which uses the raw internal `BacklogItem.sections` storage key verbatim (snake_case, e.g. `impact_radius`) rather than a Title-Case display string. A literal lookup on `sections[\\\"Impact Radius\\\"]` against that response never matches any key, regardless of whether the section name is registered in `SECTION_HEADING`.\\n\\nImpact: `groom-drift.md`'s Mode B drift classification and `feasibility-gate.md`'s BLOCKED effort/priority-mismatch check may silently find no data for a title-selector `backlog view` call, since the key format the docs describe doesn't match what the tool actually returns for that call shape.\\n\\nReference: found during PR #2964 review while verifying that a related storage-key-normalization fix covered these two consumers.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **groom-drift.md and feasibility-gate.md reference sections[] by title-case display string, but backlog_view returns snake_case keys for title-selector items** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input (PR #2964 review, discovered while verifying normalize-on-read consumer coverage)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a1264eae0b00417ab4857275081de210586e0eae17ee927c1e3c44bf4b0ca643\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgwM-g\"}"}